From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 11:01:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] kernel: make UDP tunnel support selectable

NET_UDP_TUNNEL has no prompt and therefore cannot be enabled directly by
the kmod-udptunnel packages. This leaves external modules such as ovpn-dco
without the UDP tunnel exports on otherwise minimal configurations.

Make the option user-selectable, matching the existing Linux 6.12 and
6.18 compatibility patches.

Signed-off-by: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>
---
 net/ipv4/Kconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/net/ipv4/Kconfig
+++ b/net/ipv4/Kconfig
@@ -315,7 +315,7 @@ config NET_IPVTI
 	  on top.
 
 config NET_UDP_TUNNEL
-	tristate
+	tristate "IP: UDP tunneling support"
 	select NET_IP_TUNNEL
 	default n
 
